There will be no additional research for seniors.
- Why is it?
According to Rafał Trzaskowski’s announcements, a program of free preventive tests for seniors aged 70 and 80 was to be introduced in Warsaw.
However, the idea will not be put into effect because it has not been approved by the Ministry ofHealth and its Subsequent Agency for the Protection of Medical Technologies and Tariffs.
In the explanatory memorandum, the agency explained that the target group was poorly matched.
“Producing activities may even result in detectability of individual sickness units, which may contribute to aggravating difficulties in access to NFZ services and negatively affect the patient, causing anxiety and discomfort associated with a falsely positive result of the tests,” it said.
The decision of the ministry is not understood by the president of the capital.
“Money is ours, we’ve predicted the money for it.
Only the government is afraid that if people get tested, they will later go to the doctor, which is absurd, because it's all about achieving a situation in which prevention can be done faster.
All specialists know that this helps when it comes to the burden of the health system, because it helps in the rapid detection of diseases and in a reliable approach to health.
“The government here has a very odd position that I don’t understand,” said Rafał Trzaskowski.
“It’s hard for me to imagine that proficipated specialists say: Let’s do not examine each other because there will be longer queues at the doctor, and if such specialists are advising the government, I’m not surprised that there is a health service in such a state.”
