Nice, at least officially refusing to comment.
Find out if you’re washing your hands well.
We all know that they need to be washed (e.g. after coming home or before a meal).
But not everyone knows that in order to actually get rid of germs, you have to do it in the right way.
It’s especially important now that autumn infections are approaching.
It will take at least 30 to 40 seconds to sufficiently remove dangerous bacteria and viruses from our hands
But most of us wash them shorter!
It’s enough to have hot water and plain soap – it’s not true that it has to be antibacterial (many doctors even advise against them).
Washing, we rub not only the bottoms and tops of the hand, but also: finger tips (combined or one-on-one) – rupeat them with circular movements on the inside of the other hand, spaces between your fingers (weave your hands, rubbing your fingers against each other), the thumbs – each thumb is covered with the other hand, and in this way we turn it to the right and left.
In an emergency situation (when it is impossible to wash our hands), we should wipe our hands with a wet handkerchief, and then use antibacterial gel (in drugstores, from 5 PLN).
After using the public toilet, do not touch the handles washed or the door (recommended by the Chief Sanitary Inspectorate).
Open it through a paper to towel.
Iranian President Says Reveals U.S. Controversy Disciplates U.S. Controversy
“Teheran did not hold talks with the U.S. website during the United Nations General Assembly in New York, despite an offer made by the Americans to lift the sanctions, Iranian President Hassan Rouhani said on Friday.
U.S. President Donald Trump has commented that it was the Iranian side who asked to lift the restrictions, which he did not agree.
According to Iranian President Hassan Rouhani, the U.S. has proposed abolishing all sanctions imposed on Tehran in exchange for negotiating a new international agreement.
It would be regulating both Iran’s nuclear program and a ballistic missile program.
Rouhani: Iran won't hold talks in an atmosphere of maximum pressure
Iran's prime minister said he did not agree to make these talks due to a “toxic atmosphere.”
He stated that he had encountered U.S. diplomats because he succumbed to France, Germany and Great Britain.
However, he stressed that Iran would not engage in talks in an atmosphere of “maximum pressure.”
“And even if we want to negotiate with the Americans in 5+1 format, no one is able to predict what the end result will be,” Rouhani said.
A day earlier, the Iranian leader said it did not exclude talks with the United States, and the European sides of the nuclear deal accused them of favoring U.S. sanctions on Iran.
“The sanctions imposed on Iran after the U.S. is a “preliminary condition that doesn’t allow” to form a dialogue.
“If we can abolish this preamble condition, and if the United States removes sanctions and maximum pressure, then of course we can talk to America.”
He added that he did not preclude a meeting with U.S. President Donald Trump, even though he did not agree to such an inter-speecheque at the U.N. General Assembly.
“Iran asked, I said no.”
Donald Trump tweeted that it was him who rejected the request of the Iranian side.
“Iran wanted me to remove the sanctions imposed on them so that we could meet.
“Of course I’ve said ‘no!’ tweeted the U.S. President.
Tension with atomic agreement in the background
France, Germany and the United Kingdom are trying to alleviate the tensions between Washington and Tehran in some form to salvage the 2015 Iran deal they were signatories.
It stipulated that in exchange for the abolition of economic sanctions, Iran would give up its nuclear weapons program, and the nuclear sector would be in control of the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA).
Since the U.S. withdrew from the agreement in May 2015, its remaining signatories have repeatedly acknowledged that they want to uphold the agreement.
It's gone so far.
“Welcomply is using the tactics of exerting maximum pressure on Iran, and the sanctions also include a full embargo on Iranian oil.
Teheran has announced that if he does not be allowed to export the raw material, every 60 days he will limit his obligations under the agreement.
