UBS: Gold near equilibrium
“The course of the euro will continue in the coming months around the PLN 4.35 level, which will be accompanied by a weak economic situation in global markets,” says Michael Bolliger from UBS Wealth Management.
“The expectation to maintain a solid pace of economic growth and stable monetary policy is in favor of stabilizing the zloty’s quotations at the current level,” the specialist says in an interview with Bankier.pl.
In his opinion, despite a clear inflationary pressure, the Monetary Policy Council will do not decide to increase rates in an environment where the vast majority of central banks allegide politics.
“While the zlot’s zloty is properly valued—euro quotations should persist in the coming months around the ceiling of PLN 4.35 – Polish bonds are not attractive.
Significantly more favorable yields than Polish securities are offered by bonds from emerging markets,” says Michael Bolliger, Head of Asset Encapsulation (EIss UBS Wealth Management).
According to the specialist, the main threat to the Polish economy is the downturn in the world.
“The global slowdown may get worse, but there shouldn’t be a severe recession, but at most there should be a d’etat of GDP growth slightly below zero,” Bolliger said.
“Investors should be insulted by global actions, which may be undermined by the lack of prospects for resolvating the U.S.-China trade conflict and other geopolitical risk factors, including the impeachment procedure of Donald Trump and Brexit.
