Communnials will teach drivers how to drive through the intersection
The police action will be carried out, among others, at the intersection of Cieplińskiego Avenue with Piłsudskiego Avenue.
The actions of the uniformed are somehow related to the recent complaints by the city authorities against drivers who are not always able to behave properly at the intersection.
On Friday, September 27, police officers begin preventive actions in Rzeszów “Przejezdne intersections”.
It’s all about eliminating traffic difficulties: driving into the intersection without the possibility of a dial/report, non-application of light signals or road signs.
“We often think that we’re alone at the intersection, and we’re actually impeding the lives of other drivers,” said Marek Ustrobiński, vice-president of the city a few days ago.
His words sounded at a press conference of the town hall, at which the authorities of the city presented examples of inadequacient movement of cars around intersections, which creates traffic jams as a result.
At that time, the president appealed to travelers for common sense on the road and, among other things, to move faster on the lights or not to write text messages while driving.
The topic has been taken over by Rzeszów policemen, who from today start the “Transparent intersections” action.
- What's the matter?
The aim of the activities is to eliminate the phenomenon of restrictiveness at intersections by drivers entering them without the ability to continue driving.
It’s a frequent offense that contributes to exacerbating obstacles in movement and collaps.
It's endangered with a fine of $300 and 2 punitive points.
In addition, the uniforms will pay attention to non-application of light signals or road signs and incorrect parking in the intersection area.
They will also monitor the lack of fluidity of the ride, the late start-up under the beacons, the free crossing of intersections and leaving too many distances between the vehicles.
At what intersections will the activities be carried out?
Among other things at Lisa-Kuli Street from Jagiellońska, al. Cieplińskiego from Piłsudskiego Avenue; ul. Targowa from Piłsudskiego Avenue; Śrewitów Square with Dąbrowski Street or Hetmańska Street from Warsaw Insurgents Avenue.
