The Senate Decided on Key Legislation
“The Senate has adopted without amendments a bill to disclose the assets of the most important civil servants of the most important in the country.
52 senators voted in favour of an enclagmentation law on the property of the families of civil servants – without amendments, 14 voted against, three abstentions.
Thus, the senators decided to discard the 12 amendments tabled during Wednesday’s Debate by Sławomir Rybicki.
According to him, the amendments had to “civilize” the law and to limit the scope provided in the statement of information on the property situation of one’s own children, the spouse’s children, children adopted for cases in which the children remain in a common household with a person obligated to make a statement.
The act on the transparency of the assets of the families of the most important public officials, whose project was created in the Prime Minister’s office, was adopted by the Sejm on September 11.
The regulations assume that, inter alia, the Prime Minister, ministries, deputies, MEPs, senators, presidents: the Constitutional Tribunal, the Supreme Administrative Court and the Supreme Court, as well as those at the head of other state institutions will be obliged to include in the property declaration information about the personal property of spouses, children and persons remaining in common life.
The Senate also did not propose amendments to the law on flights of the most important people in the state.
It regulates what flights have HEAD status and who may be aboard the government aircraft along with the most important people in the state.
The Act also clarifies who is responsible for running the Central Flight Register.
Fifty-three senators voted in favour of the bill without amendments, 12 against and four abstained.
According to the law, every flight of the president will be a flight “executed in an official mission”.
The president’s flights will be able to be accompanied by family members and other people invited by the president.
On the other hand, the flight in the official mission of the Prime Minister and the Marshals of the Sejm and the Senate will be only a flight “used in order to carry out tasks directly related to the performed function”.
It also speculsifies a list of people who can accompany the most important people in the country during the flight.
According to the regulations, there may be members of the delegation – invited deputies, senators, representatives of public authorities and experts; persons providing technical, medical or organisational services, as well as journalists.
In accordance with the Act, in the case of doubts related to the flights of Marshals of the Sejm and the Senate, the head of the KPRM will request their clarification.
If such doubts are not clarified at the appointed time, the head of KPRM will be obliged to notify the heads of the Chancellery of the Sejm or the Senate about the inability to organize such a flight.
