The names of foreign cities on road signs also in Polish
GDDKiA is planning to replace the signage on the entire managed road network by the end of 2020.
the GDDKiA Rzeszów
In Podkarpacie, the implementation of an amendment to the Regulation of the Ministry of Infrastructure has begun to be carried out on, among other things, the registration of the names of foreign cities on road signs also in Polish.
"Lviv" appears next to "L'viv".
In our voivodeship the changes will be introduced on 94 road signs set at the A4 motorway and national roads: DK19, DK94.
As we hear, it’s going to be easier, clear and simpler.
The new guidelines result from an amendment to the Regulation of the Minister of Infrastructure on specific technical conditions for road signs and signals and road safety devices.
“We should bear in mind that the names of towns in neighboring countries often also have a Polish sound.
Thanks to the change prepared by us in the law, they will finally appear on the signs on our roads.
Introducing a new signage is started from the Podkarpackie section of the A4 motorway”, informed the Minister of Infrastructure Andrzej Adamczyk.
In Podkarpacie, changes will be introduced on 94 road signs set at the A4 motorway and national roads: DK19, DK94.
The total cost of the investment?
$200,000.
In the first place, the new signage will be implemented on the A4 motorway, which is planned by November 1, 2019.
And what should the implementation of the idea look like?
It's going to happen without excretion of boards, on the principle of stickers.
They will replace the currently functioning names of localities with new ones, written in the Polish language on the already existing signs.
The two names will be written in one row – in the first place in Polish, and then in the original, in parentheses.
It will be a great facilitation for people who do not know the chinctuation of the names of foreign cities in the language of the country in which they are located.
Feel the Game with Razer Nari Ultimate for Xbox One
Razer Announced Razer Nari Ultimate for Xbox One, the world’s first headset powered by haptic technology.
HyperSense provides immersion in games and provides better control over your surroundings.
Razer HyperSense uses haptic solutions developed by Lofelt, a German company specializing in developing advanced haptic technologies that provide a realistic touch-based experience.
HyperSense employs Special Haptic Controllers and Smart Digital Signal Transmitter to Generate High-Reambiguous Reliquid Coupling in real-time, allowing you to fully immerse yourself in every game on Xbox One.
The technology recognizes the sound signals and converts them into dynamic vibrations, allowing players to escalate the gameplay without having to install additional software.
By utilizing the sense of touch, sound signals can accurately imitate actions in the game.
Razer HyperSense reproduces events—from silent footsteps to powerful explosions, fine-tuning all activities around the player.
“Nari Ultimate for Xbox One has been designed to give all players an additional gameplay dimension.
“With HyperSense, we’re letting them immerse each other completely in their favorite titles,” said Alvin Cheung Senior Vice President, Razer’s Peripheral Equipment.
Swivel cushions are equipped with cushions filled with foam with shape memory and cooling gel layer, in order to reduce the heat generated during long use.
For an even easier operation of headphones, a quick mute button was placed on the retractable microphone, and the HyperSense intensity controller and a balance slider between the game and the hut on the headphone case.
Self-adapting to the shape of the head-shape, the headband ensures trouble-free and accurate matching.
In addition, Razer Nari Ultimate for Xbox One has an Xbox Wireless feature that lets you directly connect to your console without the need for a wireless transceiver, allowing for easy and quick setup.
Headphones also support Windows Sonic for a more realistic sound.
Razer Nari Ultimate, originally earmarked for PC, debuted in September 2018.
With Nari Ultimate for Xbox One, Razer can now offer this award-winning technology to Xbox One fans.
Set was valued at EUR 219.99.
