Gowin: “we have to arouse the Polish little trade”
“Effective taxation of hyper-markets does not solve the problem of small commerce, it will be necessary to consider whether the state has any instruments to stimulate Polish trade,” Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Science and Higher Education and the Leader of the Agreement Jarosław Gowin said on Friday.
Gowin, during a conversation in "Signals of the day" on Radio One, stated that the trade is overwhelmed by multinational networks, which imposing such low margins on Polish producers that practically Polish companies can not develop.
Recognizing that it is very difficult to fight this problem, the Deputy Prime Minister reminded that the PiS government tried to deal with it at the very beginning of the term, but received a “account on the part of the European Commission”.
“We have won before the tribunal of justice and I hope that if the United Right wins the next election and the government is forming, we will come back to this topic,” he said.
“Effective taxation of hyper-markets does not solve the problem of the Polish, i.e. small-to-trary”.
“Therefore we will have to consider whether the government, the state has any instruments to stimulate Polish trade,” Gowin said.
In May, an EU court decided that the European Commission made a mistake recognizing that the Polish retail tax is illegitimate public aid.
The Retail Sales Tax Act assumed the introduction of two trade tax rates: 0.8 per cent on income between PLN 17 million and PLN 170 million per month and 1.4 per cent on income above PLN 170 million per month.
The tax came in effect from September 2016.
In September 2016, the European Commission initiated proceedings for infringement of EU law by Poland.
At that time, Brussels argued that the design of the tax could favour smaller stores, which could be considered public aid.
She later stated that the levocation was put into effect in an unlawful manner.
It also issued an injunction to suspend the application of the tax p.m. pending its analysis by officials in Brussels.
Poland did not agree with this position, but tax collection has been suspended.
The European Court’s May decision has paved the way for reincorporation of the tax, but it has not ended the case.
On 24 July the Commission filed an appeal at the Court of Justice.
On Thursday, the CJEU’s press services told PAP that the case is currently at a written stage in which both the European Commission and the Polish government present their arguments in writing.
It is not yet known whether and when the oral procedure, i.e. listening to the parties and a possible dissertation.
It takes a good few to several months from the filing of annunciation to announce the veri veri verdict.
“Such proceedings take an average of one year,” a source at the Court of Luxembourg told PAP.
How to Dress Your Child for Baptism?
Suppose several practical solutions
Baptism is an extremely important celebration in the life of an infant and their parents.
It’s also often the first opportunity where the whole family is centered around the child, together celebrating its appearance in the world.
It’s no wonder, therefore, that the newly minted mother and dad want their children to look the best on that day.
However, before you also make a final decision about the baby’s outfit, consider whether it will also be comfortable.
You can find a lot of attire sets in the stores, which do not provide the toddler with proper comfort.
So what should you pay attention to?
The basic criterion for the selection of clothes for baptism is the child's age
Until recently, several-kilometrous toddlers were baptized, troggled in white sets and put into the same bars or large pod cushions.
Today, children who come to the sacrament are often the elders: several-fuses, australic, and even larger.
It’s not hard to figure out that such a big consolation already needs a slightly different christening garment to be baptized.
Therefore, if your child is 3–4 months on the day of Baptism, he will probably spend the ceremony in a wheelchair or on the hands of her parents or godparents.
The best way to do it will turn out to decorate it with comfortable, cotton sleepers or sets.
Although this wardrobe element is considered an everyday attire, it is enough to find its festive variants, for example with a frill or lace.
For the boy it will turn out to be an ideal body with printing flies and harnesses.
In the case of older children, you can afford a greater fantasy in your clothes.
The little-chief will look beautiful in a simple, tulle dress
The many parents of the girls are eagerly looking towards richly adorned, bridle dresses for baptism complete with coats, wristbands and hats.
“Unfortunately, a large number of manufacturers for their product use artificial, non-breathing materials in which the child is simply inconvenient.
In search of a suitable garment, it would be better to look at the Asanti for Kids store, which offers elegant outfits on cotton linings.
Delicate tulle skirts, satin dresses, laces, appliances and cute sets will make your daughter look beautiful and feel comfortable.
Perfect outfit for a small gentleman: a cotton suit
Until recently, among the children’s parents there was a fashion for suits, a copy of “adult” models.
Polyester jackets and trousers, rigid collars or casskets often made young elegants loudly demonstrate their dissatisfaction.
Today, fortunately they have been supplanted by comfortable cotton sets.
It is enough to take a look at the sets available in the Asanti for Kids, i.e. soft sweatpants, and the blouse is decorated on the front with a velvet pattern.
These costumes look extremely festive, and at the same time do not embarrassing the movements of the toddler.
