“Superwizjera” TVN journalists disclosed that Marian Banaś, the president of the Supreme Chamber of Inspection, in recent recent years did not include a 400-metre tenement house, which is located in the Podgórze district of Krakow.
What’s more, his sub-leather was supposed to be a sex business in the aforementioned tenement house (i.e. rent rooms for hours).
On the other hand, the building itself has allegedly been a collateral for the repayment of the loan since 2016.
Bertold Kittel drew attention to irregularities in the “Superwizjer” program.
A journalist has revealed that Banasia’s tenement house was rented by people tied to the criminal world to use it as a place of “erotic meetings.”
The clients were supposed to be men using the services of prostitutes.
