Interestingly, a tenant-leased tenement house led the journalist to uncover negligence in Banasia’s property statements.
The tenement house itself was vaguely described in them, and the income from its rental was to be underestimated.
“Memitek of Marian Banasia and his wife may be worth PLN 6 to $8 million.
In total, the spouses can boast of two houses, three apartments, savings[...]”, writes Money.pl.
And, according to the analysis of the portal, the Banasia tenement house itself was already worth about PLN 3 million.
The Central Anti-Corruption Bureau is currently auditing Marian Banaś’s property statements for the years 2015–2019.
Banaś announced that by the time it was completed, it will suspend its activities at NIK. “I will apply to the Marshal for unretribution,” he said.
